    "values": {
      "summary": "Replace Runtime v3 kernel flat-file checkpoint and lifelog persistence with one redb-backed durable state boundary for local adapters and governed operations.",
      "actual_changes": [
        "Added a narrow Runtime v3 redb durable-state module with local checkpoint, local lifelog, governed state, and governed lifelog tables.",
        "Moved local CheckpointStore and Lifelog adapters from checkpoint.json/lifelog.jsonl to immediate redb transactions with identity and integrity validation.",
        "Moved governed Runtime v3 checkpoint and lifelog persistence from flat files to the shared redb store while preserving gate, replay, shutdown, and redaction behavior.",
        "Fail closed when legacy flat checkpoint/lifelog persistence files are present in a configured state root.",
        "Updated focused tests to prove restart, corruption rejection, identity partitioning, durable lifelog, and absence of legacy flat persistence."
      ],
